1
00:00:13,474 --> 00:00:15,034
Good cake...

2
00:00:21,754 --> 00:00:24,014
What a pitiful sight.

3
00:00:31,524 --> 00:00:33,154
Iorogi.

4
00:00:41,634 --> 00:00:44,774
Kobato.

5
00:00:44,774 --> 00:00:47,614
Kobato.
Dou sureba iin dakke?

6
00:00:47,614 --> 00:00:52,014
Kobato.
Atarimae no kototte itsumo

7
00:00:52,914 --> 00:00:56,214
Muzukashii na

8
00:00:56,214 --> 00:00:58,984
Ureshii toki waratte

9
00:00:58,984 --> 00:01:03,284
Suki na toki ni utaitai dake

10
00:01:03,864 --> 00:01:06,294
Na no ni

11
00:01:07,594 --> 00:01:11,964
Itsuka negai wa kanau to

12
00:01:12,404 --> 00:01:15,674
Demo "itsuka" tte dore kurai?

13
00:01:15,674 --> 00:01:19,164
Machikirenai yo

14
00:01:19,304 --> 00:01:25,084
123! no aizu de ryoute hirogete

15
00:01:25,084 --> 00:01:30,284
Zenshin ni hikari wo atsumete

16
00:01:30,284 --> 00:01:33,124
Doko ni aru no?

17
00:01:33,124 --> 00:01:36,454
Oshiete, watashi ni dekiru koto

18
00:01:36,454 --> 00:01:39,294
Meippai kizu tsuite

19
00:01:39,294 --> 00:01:42,194
Seiippai hashitte

20
00:01:42,194 --> 00:01:46,164
Nan juu kai koronde naite

21
00:01:46,164 --> 00:01:49,204
Sore de mo mada

22
00:01:49,204 --> 00:01:53,234
Akireru kurai

23
00:01:53,714 --> 00:01:57,874
Ashita wo shinjiteru

24
00:02:07,624 --> 00:02:13,064
...Silver Eyes.

25
00:02:18,434 --> 00:02:20,464
Hey! It's Kobato!

26
00:02:20,574 --> 00:02:22,404
Good morning Kobato!

27
00:02:22,404 --> 00:02:23,994
Good morning.

28
00:02:24,504 --> 00:02:28,374
Kobato, can I put a ribbon on your doll?

29
00:02:28,874 --> 00:02:30,034
My doll?

30
00:02:30,744 --> 00:02:32,234
Oh, you mean Ioryogi-san?

31
00:02:33,014 --> 00:02:35,214
Oh hey come on, give me a break.

32
00:02:35,554 --> 00:02:37,414
Yes, please!

33
00:02:42,754 --> 00:02:44,194
How cute!

34
00:02:44,524 --> 00:02:47,294
Yes. Ioryogi-san is happy, too.

35
00:02:47,294 --> 00:02:49,094
What makes you think I'm happy?!

36
00:02:52,704 --> 00:02:54,194
Good morning.

37
00:02:54,404 --> 00:02:56,034
Good morning, Kobato.

38
00:02:56,504 --> 00:02:57,874
Thanks for your help, as always.

39
00:02:57,874 --> 00:02:58,964
Yes.

40
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:06,774
Well, I've got to go now, Ioryogi-san.

41
00:03:14,254 --> 00:03:16,744
Why does she insist on carrying
that thing around?

42
00:03:17,424 --> 00:03:19,524
It's probably very important to her.

43
00:03:26,104 --> 00:03:29,374
So delicious

44
00:03:29,374 --> 00:03:29,704
Bear's Baumkuchen Shop
So delicious

45
00:03:29,704 --> 00:03:29,874
Bear's Baumkuchen Shop

46
00:03:29,874 --> 00:03:31,304
Bear's Baumkuchen Shop
Baumkuchen

47
00:03:31,304 --> 00:03:32,344
Bear's Baumkuchen Shop
Baked to perfection

48
00:03:32,344 --> 00:03:32,564
Baked to perfection

49
00:03:32,974 --> 00:03:34,374
Baked to perfection

50
00:03:34,644 --> 00:03:37,474
Oh, yes Perfection

51
00:03:38,284 --> 00:03:41,974
Freshly baked by the bear from the woods

52
00:03:43,954 --> 00:03:45,254
You're an eyesore.

53
00:03:45,454 --> 00:03:46,954
Come on, get inside.

54
00:03:46,954 --> 00:03:48,184
Ginsei.

55
00:03:51,924 --> 00:03:53,794
I'll tell you, he's not here.

56
00:03:54,394 --> 00:03:55,594
I know that.

57
00:03:55,994 --> 00:03:57,764
Then what brings you here?

58
00:03:58,534 --> 00:04:02,934
I just want to know what's on his mind.

59
00:04:03,204 --> 00:04:04,734
Why are you asking me?

60
00:04:05,904 --> 00:04:07,034
Never mind.

61
00:04:07,474 --> 00:04:11,644
We appear like this now,
but we are from Ikai.

62
00:04:11,844 --> 00:04:12,914
Why bring that up now?

63
00:04:12,914 --> 00:04:15,184
Well then, what was the
initiative in us being here?

64
00:04:15,684 --> 00:04:20,714
There are four worlds: "Tenkai,"
"Ningenkai," "Chikai" and "Ikai."

65
00:04:21,954 --> 00:04:24,984
The only ones who are not conscious
of there being different worlds

66
00:04:25,224 --> 00:04:27,324
are the humans from "Ningenkai."

67
00:04:28,834 --> 00:04:32,354
In Tenkai there are angels,
who are under God's rule.

68
00:04:33,974 --> 00:04:37,964
Demons follow the Devil's rule in Chikai.

69
00:04:39,604 --> 00:04:44,374
And in Ikai, where we are from, we have our
master, "Kototonushi" to bow down to.

70
00:04:47,214 --> 00:04:52,174
In each world, nonaggression is the rule
of thumb. But look at that fool Iorogi.

71
00:04:54,754 --> 00:04:57,694
Okay, okay, that little bit of a fool Iorogi.

72
00:04:58,624 --> 00:05:02,794
If he hadn't started a war with Tenkai,
we wouldn't all be in this mess.

73
00:05:06,204 --> 00:05:08,934
The reason Iorogi went to war with Tenkai

74
00:05:09,804 --> 00:05:13,074
was because there was something there
that he wanted, no matter what.

75
00:05:14,144 --> 00:05:15,574
But...

76
00:05:15,674 --> 00:05:17,644
He never got it.

77
00:05:18,314 --> 00:05:23,684
That's right. He should've just gone and stolen
it, just like that son of the Devil in Chikai did.

78
00:05:24,884 --> 00:05:30,154
So we end up losing, and the dude gets turned
into a doll for breaking the Nonaggression Act.

79
00:05:30,524 --> 00:05:36,154
I become the bear with a Baumkuchen shop, and
Zuisho gets turned into a silly-looking bird.

80
00:05:37,604 --> 00:05:41,164
Just goes to show that even the amazing
"God" can get fed up at times.

81
00:05:42,334 --> 00:05:46,144
I mean, we got it pretty bad,
but as the mastermind,

82
00:05:46,144 --> 00:05:47,704
he's definitely in the toughest position.

83
00:05:48,544 --> 00:05:51,474
What must Iorogi do to return to Ikai?

84
00:05:52,584 --> 00:05:57,144
Until that girl's wish comes true,
he'll remain in that form,

85
00:05:57,254 --> 00:05:58,814
and he won't be able to return to Ikai.

86
00:05:59,224 --> 00:06:00,314
Wish?

87
00:06:02,494 --> 00:06:06,994
After she has filled her bottle with
broken human hearts she had healed,

88
00:06:06,994 --> 00:06:10,264
then her dream will come true.

89
00:06:11,404 --> 00:06:14,304
Iorogi's job is to help her.
That was his promise to "God".

90
00:06:15,874 --> 00:06:18,364
I have no idea what he's thinking.

91
00:06:19,104 --> 00:06:23,734
Well, one thing I can say though, is that
since Iorogi arrived at Ningenkai...

92
00:06:24,414 --> 00:06:29,284
You see, since he started hanging
around with that girl, he's changed.

93
00:06:30,184 --> 00:06:32,014
Just leave him alone for awhile.

94
00:06:32,454 --> 00:06:33,884
Come on, have some of this.

95
00:06:37,624 --> 00:06:38,884
Darn.

96
00:06:40,694 --> 00:06:41,954
He doesn't know what he's missing.

97
00:06:43,964 --> 00:06:46,954
If my old friends saw me like this, they'd cry!

98
00:06:50,944 --> 00:06:52,234
Oh?

99
00:07:05,284 --> 00:07:07,624
Come and get me if you can.

100
00:07:07,924 --> 00:07:10,014
Kobato. Good morning.

101
00:07:11,094 --> 00:07:12,524
Domoto!

102
00:07:14,294 --> 00:07:15,864
What brings you to the kindergarten?

103
00:07:15,864 --> 00:07:18,234
I came to see Fujimoto.

104
00:07:18,434 --> 00:07:19,424
Huh?

105
00:07:20,064 --> 00:07:22,094
Time for lunch, everybody.

106
00:07:22,204 --> 00:07:23,704
Wash your hands and get inside!

107
00:07:23,704 --> 00:07:25,004
Okay!

108
00:07:25,004 --> 00:07:26,094
Fujimoto.

109
00:07:27,574 --> 00:07:29,164
What are you doing here?

110
00:07:29,414 --> 00:07:33,284
I came to get you. I think it would be
good to attend today's seminar.

111
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:35,584
I'm not going.

112
00:07:35,584 --> 00:07:37,784
But you took it because you wanted to.

113
00:07:38,124 --> 00:07:40,054
Um... What's a seminar?

114
00:07:40,254 --> 00:07:42,654
It's a class at university.

115
00:07:42,654 --> 00:07:45,054
Oh. University studies.

116
00:07:45,364 --> 00:07:46,424
Mhm.

117
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:48,294
You missed the last one too.

118
00:07:48,734 --> 00:07:50,324
You really should go today.

119
00:07:50,904 --> 00:07:52,764
Please go, Fujimoto!

120
00:07:53,304 --> 00:07:55,034
I can't. I'm too busy.

121
00:07:59,844 --> 00:08:00,944
Fujimoto!

122
00:08:00,944 --> 00:08:02,344
Kobato...

123
00:08:02,474 --> 00:08:05,074
Don't worry about it. I have a plan.

124
00:08:05,814 --> 00:08:06,804
Huh?

125
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:11,674
That's enough for today.

126
00:08:11,854 --> 00:08:14,054
You've got an important seminar
in the afternoon, don't you?

127
00:08:14,054 --> 00:08:15,314
Ms. Sayaka

128
00:08:16,024 --> 00:08:19,224
I've helped out here on a number of occasions.

129
00:08:19,924 --> 00:08:21,624
I realized something on one of those occasions.

130
00:08:22,134 --> 00:08:25,664
The children will be taking a nap in the
afternoon anyway and Kobato is here to help.

131
00:08:25,664 --> 00:08:26,704
We'll be all right.

132
00:08:26,704 --> 00:08:27,764
However...

133
00:08:27,834 --> 00:08:29,134
Fujimoto.

134
00:08:29,434 --> 00:08:31,204
You always are a tremendous help.

135
00:08:32,044 --> 00:08:35,204
But you know, I don't want you
skipping classes at university.

136
00:08:36,714 --> 00:08:38,204
Will you do that?

137
00:08:39,014 --> 00:08:40,244
Sure.

138
00:08:40,514 --> 00:08:42,284
He listens to her.

139
00:08:42,284 --> 00:08:46,314
He'll do whatever Ms. Sayaka says. Only her.

140
00:08:48,154 --> 00:08:51,214
I cannot be seen wearing this dreamy girly thing!

141
00:09:12,114 --> 00:09:14,544
Bye for now, Kobato. I'll visit you again.

142
00:09:14,714 --> 00:09:16,984
Yes. Please come again.

143
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:19,584
See you.

144
00:09:22,454 --> 00:09:24,394
Have a nice afternoon!

145
00:09:28,594 --> 00:09:31,224
Kobato is ready to cover for Fujimoto too!

146
00:09:43,044 --> 00:09:45,474
Wow, that's wonderful!

147
00:09:51,784 --> 00:09:57,314
Darn, I can't get it off! That Fujimoto!
He tied it too tight!

148
00:10:27,324 --> 00:10:31,314
Thank you so much for today, Kobato.
It really helped to have you around.

149
00:10:31,664 --> 00:10:33,214
N-No problem!

150
00:10:33,364 --> 00:10:35,594
Now go home and get some rest, okay?

151
00:10:35,934 --> 00:10:37,294
Yes!

152
00:10:38,004 --> 00:10:40,624
That ribbon looks very nice on little Ioryogi.

153
00:10:43,334 --> 00:10:45,674
"Little" Ioryogi?

154
00:10:47,844 --> 00:10:50,434
Yes! See you tomorrow!

155
00:10:59,124 --> 00:11:01,284
It's still a bit hot, isn't it?

156
00:11:07,934 --> 00:11:10,454
It's cooler where there is dirt.

157
00:11:14,874 --> 00:11:18,394
It feels good doesn't it, Ioryogi-san?

158
00:11:24,444 --> 00:11:26,384
Hey! What are you doing?!

159
00:11:26,844 --> 00:11:29,844
You're all squished right here.

160
00:11:31,054 --> 00:11:32,914
You know why?

161
00:11:33,084 --> 00:11:35,184
Because you're hungry?

162
00:11:47,304 --> 00:11:48,734
Kobato...

163
00:11:50,604 --> 00:11:53,164
The seasons continue to change, you know.

164
00:11:53,744 --> 00:11:58,514
You didn't come here to help out at
the kindergarten, did you?

165
00:12:01,584 --> 00:12:08,224
But today, Fujimoto wasn't there so I
wanted to do my best to cover for him.

166
00:12:08,224 --> 00:12:11,814
You do what you're supposed to be doing
before talking about such things!

167
00:12:14,694 --> 00:12:20,534
Unless you quickly fill this bottle,
your wish isn't going to come true.

168
00:12:31,614 --> 00:12:32,814
Ginsei...

169
00:12:32,814 --> 00:12:34,974
Is he your friend, Ioryogi-san?

170
00:12:48,994 --> 00:12:50,554
Ioryogi-san?!

171
00:12:53,034 --> 00:12:54,504
So she's the one!

172
00:12:55,934 --> 00:12:56,904
Kobato!

173
00:13:17,524 --> 00:13:19,114
Ioryogi-san?

174
00:13:45,754 --> 00:13:47,744
Oh, could that be?

175
00:13:56,334 --> 00:14:00,734
Man... if you break that...
I'll never forgive you...!

176
00:14:01,934 --> 00:14:03,094
Why is that?

177
00:14:04,344 --> 00:14:08,804
Why do you stay in Ningenkai for
so long, looking like that?

178
00:14:12,114 --> 00:14:13,804
I've got things to do.

179
00:14:26,264 --> 00:14:28,124
Master Genko!

180
00:14:28,934 --> 00:14:33,394
Zuisho! Would you quit flapping around in the
shop? You'll get feathers into the dough!

181
00:14:33,764 --> 00:14:37,134
Well sir, I'm a bird now. I can't help it.

182
00:14:37,504 --> 00:14:39,704
All right, all right.

183
00:14:39,804 --> 00:14:40,774
So what is it?

184
00:14:40,774 --> 00:14:42,244
Oh that's right!

185
00:14:42,244 --> 00:14:45,784
There's a dangerous situation developing
between that violent, selfish,

186
00:14:45,784 --> 00:14:47,484
turned into some sort of doll guy

187
00:14:47,484 --> 00:14:51,614
and the problem maker who used
to work for him, sir!

188
00:14:52,284 --> 00:14:54,184
Oh. Is that so.

189
00:14:54,324 --> 00:14:55,914
Huh? That's it?

190
00:14:56,894 --> 00:14:58,484
Well then take this.

191
00:14:58,564 --> 00:15:00,584
Give it to the one that loses. For condolence.

192
00:15:00,794 --> 00:15:04,894
Are you going to let them go at it?
They're really going to cause a ruckus.

193
00:15:05,664 --> 00:15:08,104
Nobody can stop those two.

194
00:15:09,504 --> 00:15:11,764
The guy was originally picked up by Iorogi.

195
00:15:12,474 --> 00:15:14,404
It was Iorogi who named him for his silver eyes.

196
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:18,934
"Gin" for silver and "sei" for being.

197
00:15:20,314 --> 00:15:24,914
I thought the name lacked thought,
so I told him to reconsider,

198
00:15:25,154 --> 00:15:27,144
but then we ended up getting into a fist fight.

199
00:15:27,624 --> 00:15:28,924
I'm not surprised.

200
00:15:29,654 --> 00:15:34,784
So he was picked up and given a name.
And that's why he dwells on Iorogi issues.

201
00:15:35,634 --> 00:15:39,064
They're going to have to settle
this one themselves.

202
00:15:55,084 --> 00:15:56,554
Return that bottle.

203
00:15:57,154 --> 00:16:01,114
Get it yourself, "Mister Ioryogi".

204
00:16:01,694 --> 00:16:04,684
Well?! You want to get barbecued right here?!

205
00:16:10,934 --> 00:16:14,304
You don't expect to keep me down for
long in your present state, do you?

206
00:16:14,304 --> 00:16:15,424
Why you!

207
00:16:15,734 --> 00:16:19,234
You're a sorry sight. Your looks and your name.

208
00:16:19,544 --> 00:16:21,634
"Ioryogi"? Give me a break.

209
00:16:24,014 --> 00:16:25,574
Io... ryo?

210
00:16:29,184 --> 00:16:30,584
I-o-ro-gi!

211
00:16:32,054 --> 00:16:33,984
I-o-ryo-gi!

212
00:16:35,094 --> 00:16:36,494
I'm telling you, it's Iorogi!

213
00:16:36,494 --> 00:16:38,994
I-o-ryo-gi?

214
00:16:38,994 --> 00:16:42,224
No! It's Ioryogi... huh?

215
00:16:43,434 --> 00:16:45,364
Right. Ioryogi-san!

216
00:16:48,274 --> 00:16:51,394
But you know, I like that name I have now.

217
00:16:52,404 --> 00:16:53,934
Anyway, give back the bottle.

218
00:16:55,744 --> 00:16:57,644
Tell me you're coming back to Ikai.

219
00:16:57,784 --> 00:17:03,654
I told you, I've got things to do. I'm not
returning... until I see it through.

220
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:07,854
It's about "the wish" isn't it?

221
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:12,094
What do you see in her?

222
00:17:14,964 --> 00:17:20,164
She has put me through
so much trouble already.

223
00:17:23,574 --> 00:17:25,764
Then get rid of her.

224
00:17:25,904 --> 00:17:26,974
What?

225
00:17:26,974 --> 00:17:28,874
If she doesn't exist, there are no more wishes.

226
00:17:28,974 --> 00:17:32,774
Then you should be able to return to Ikai.

227
00:17:33,584 --> 00:17:35,644
In the past, you would have done that.

228
00:17:37,284 --> 00:17:38,414
You're probably right.

229
00:17:38,824 --> 00:17:41,914
She's really clumsy and has no common sense.

230
00:17:42,794 --> 00:17:44,784
Kobato is ready!

231
00:17:45,964 --> 00:17:48,724
She always thinks of herself last.

232
00:17:49,264 --> 00:17:52,164
She'll bend over backwards and exhaust
herself doing things for others

233
00:17:52,164 --> 00:17:54,224
that she hasn't even been asked to do.

234
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,094
But you know...

235
00:17:56,874 --> 00:18:00,464
That ridiculous personality of hers...

236
00:18:00,844 --> 00:18:02,204
I kind of like that about her.

237
00:18:08,254 --> 00:18:09,914
I can't bear to hear of it.

238
00:18:09,914 --> 00:18:12,684
Watch it! My insides are going to come out!

239
00:18:13,154 --> 00:18:17,284
If "the bottle" does not get filled,
the wish will not come true.

240
00:18:18,024 --> 00:18:19,254
Ginsei!

241
00:18:19,824 --> 00:18:22,794
In that case, if there was no bottle...

242
00:18:23,434 --> 00:18:24,664
Don't do it!

243
00:18:29,374 --> 00:18:32,304
I cannot bring myself to obey
you the way you are now!

244
00:18:34,844 --> 00:18:36,034
Ginsei!

245
00:18:36,344 --> 00:18:37,504
I'm begging you!

246
00:18:39,814 --> 00:18:41,974
Please give me back the bottle.

247
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:47,354
Without that, Kobato...

248
00:18:48,924 --> 00:18:50,394
Please.

249
00:18:52,264 --> 00:18:56,394
Since he started hanging around
with that girl, he's changed.

250
00:18:59,964 --> 00:19:01,664
You're begging me?

251
00:19:04,704 --> 00:19:07,734
You would never have said that before.

252
00:19:25,294 --> 00:19:27,284
Fulfill your objectives quickly.

253
00:19:29,694 --> 00:19:31,394
Ginsei...

254
00:19:35,574 --> 00:19:37,694
Ioryogi-san!

255
00:19:39,944 --> 00:19:41,044
Kobato!

256
00:19:41,044 --> 00:19:42,304
Kohaku!

257
00:19:42,614 --> 00:19:44,164
What's the matter?

258
00:19:44,584 --> 00:19:46,984
Ioryogi-san is gone!

259
00:19:48,084 --> 00:19:52,114
I saw Ioryogi-san at Sakura Park.

260
00:19:53,924 --> 00:19:56,354
Come and get me, if you can.

261
00:19:56,354 --> 00:19:57,954
Why, you!

262
00:19:58,224 --> 00:20:02,694
He seemed to be having so much fun
playing tag with his friend from Ikai,

263
00:20:02,694 --> 00:20:04,594
so I didn't say hello.

264
00:20:05,434 --> 00:20:08,634
Sakura Park? Thank you very much!

265
00:20:09,934 --> 00:20:11,734
You're welcome.

266
00:20:23,514 --> 00:20:25,984
Damn! What a useless body!

267
00:20:26,084 --> 00:20:27,984
But I've come this far, so...

268
00:20:43,134 --> 00:20:45,124
You're hurting me, idiot!

269
00:20:46,004 --> 00:20:48,104
Ioryogi-san!

270
00:20:50,544 --> 00:20:55,314
Ioryogi-san! Where are you?!

271
00:20:56,184 --> 00:20:58,214
Ioryogi-san!

272
00:20:59,154 --> 00:21:00,414
Hey!

273
00:21:01,994 --> 00:21:03,384
Fujimoto?!

274
00:21:05,994 --> 00:21:06,894
Here.

275
00:21:07,064 --> 00:21:08,464
Ioryogi-san!

276
00:21:09,294 --> 00:21:11,734
What a relief, Ioryogi-san.

277
00:21:12,834 --> 00:21:16,434
Thank you very much for
finding Ioryogi-san for me.

278
00:21:16,434 --> 00:21:18,234
Ah, right.

279
00:21:19,074 --> 00:21:21,944
Ioryogi-san got himself lost.

280
00:21:22,774 --> 00:21:23,714
Lost?

281
00:21:23,714 --> 00:21:26,734
I'm so glad nothing happened to him.

282
00:21:27,584 --> 00:21:30,244
Is that doll that important to you?

283
00:21:30,984 --> 00:21:35,214
Yes! Ioryogi-san and I are always together!

284
00:21:39,394 --> 00:21:40,954
This is good!

285
00:21:43,364 --> 00:21:45,454
That bear is really thoughtful.

286
00:21:52,944 --> 00:21:54,604
It looks very nice on you!

287
00:21:55,114 --> 00:21:56,444
Why, you...

288
00:21:56,444 --> 00:21:57,814
Ioryogi-san.

289
00:21:59,244 --> 00:22:04,344
Thank you so much for getting the bottle back.

290
00:22:04,554 --> 00:22:05,984
I'm very thankful.

291
00:22:07,724 --> 00:22:09,284
Dobato!

292
00:22:10,754 --> 00:22:12,244
Minus two-hundred points!

293
00:22:12,764 --> 00:22:14,124
What?!

294
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:17,924
How could you let that precious
bottle be stolen! Get a grip!

295
00:22:18,564 --> 00:22:20,194
I'm sorry.

296
00:22:23,274 --> 00:22:29,214
What is it, "fancy day" today?! Why does
everyone want to tie a ribbon to me?!

297
00:22:30,674 --> 00:22:33,804
Ioryogi-san and I are always together!

298
00:22:39,824 --> 00:22:40,984
Ioryogi-san?

299
00:22:41,154 --> 00:22:42,124
What is it?

300
00:22:42,124 --> 00:22:44,624
I still think that ribbon looks good on you.

301
00:22:44,624 --> 00:22:45,694
It does not look good on me!

302
00:22:45,694 --> 00:22:49,494
That's not true! Look! Tie another
one and you look even...

303
00:22:49,664 --> 00:22:50,894
No, stop it!

304
00:22:50,894 --> 00:22:52,604
And tie another one, and...

305
00:22:52,604 --> 00:22:54,624
I'm telling you to cut that out!

306
00:22:54,804 --> 00:22:56,774
Oh? Then let's try one more.

307
00:23:01,314 --> 00:23:08,944
Hito wa mina tonde mitai no ni

308
00:23:10,114 --> 00:23:16,214
Juuryoku ni damasareterunda

309
00:23:16,494 --> 00:23:24,334
Dare mo honto wa toberunda yo

310
00:23:26,564 --> 00:23:32,904
Ano ko ga anna ni kanashisou na no wa

311
00:23:33,944 --> 00:23:36,814
Jibun no kage wo

312
00:23:36,814 --> 00:23:43,944
Dokoka ni wasurete kichatta kara kamo

313
00:23:44,114 --> 00:23:46,644
Sore nara

314
00:23:46,824 --> 00:23:50,924
"Arigatou," tte kimi ni ietara

315
00:23:50,924 --> 00:23:54,794
"Arigatou," tte kimi ga waraeba

316
00:23:54,794 --> 00:24:02,134
Ittari kitari ureshiku naru

317
00:24:02,674 --> 00:24:06,904
Kimi ga shiawase ni naru

318
00:24:07,204 --> 00:24:11,444
Shinpai nante iranai yo

319
00:24:11,444 --> 00:24:15,544
Issho ni iru kara

320
00:24:17,314 --> 00:24:23,254
Ureshikuttemo namida ga deru nante

321
00:24:23,254 --> 00:24:26,094
Fushigi da

322
00:24:26,094 --> 00:24:28,994
Next episode
...Angel and the Protector.
Fushigi da

323
00:24:28,994 --> 00:24:30,764
Next episode
...Angel and the Protector.

